kbook:Chicken|chicken]] pieces\n*250 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] (8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]], coarsely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*125 g (4 oz) [[Cookbook:Bacon|bacon]], coarsely chopped\n*10 [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]]\n*3 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], peeled and minced\n*45 g (1½ oz) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*1 bottle [[Cookbook:Red Wine|red wine]]\n*3 sprigs [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n*1 sprig [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]]\n*Chopped parsley, for [[Cookbook:Garnish|garnish]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 180°C (350°F).\n#Remove the skin from the chicken. Season all the pieces.\n#Pour the oil into a flame-proof casserole.\n#[[Cookbook:Rendering|Render]] the bacon and add the onions.\n#Add garlic, the mushrooms, and then the chicken. Add the wine and herbs.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for about 45 minutes.\n#Several minutes before the end of the cooking period, add the flour mixed with the olive oil to the liquid in the casserole, and mix well, turning the chicken pieces to coat well with the sauce.\n#Sprinkle the chicken with chopped parsley before serving.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mushroom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wine]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:French recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Alsatian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bacon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Alsatian Chicken Fricassée","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 kg (4 lbs) chicken pieces","sourceText":"2 kg (4 lbs) chic